  designNotes: "Beat 5: fight upward. The platform garrison cannot be reached on
    a flat arc, so the drag has to be lofted \u2014 the first level where the ANGLE
    matters more than the power. NO PLAYER TANK (2026-08-21): the three shells
    were the structure-killer (96x3=288) and turned the loft into a 3-shell errand.
    Crew folded into the ground line (2+5 -> 7). HP not retuned yet \u2014 win is
    units dead, so the loft onto the platform is the beat; if the tower then reads
    as a wall, cut hpScale before inventing a shop. Bunker moved 1.8 -> 5.0; at 11.3
    the separation was the worst in the campaign. Rule 7 used to warn because the
    tank crew (back rank) could not reach the platform; without them the warning
    may clear. Structure hp RETUNED 2026-08-07: bunker hpScale 0.55 (250 -> 137).
    Tower garrison 2026-08-21: those were MACHINE GUNNERS (6 crowd), not snipers.
    MG belong in the street (3, at 3.5). ONE sniper on the platform \u2014 elevated,
    back, hard to reach. The loft is still the beat; the payload is one 16-hp gun,
    not a roof of burst fire."
